Subject: v3: reads confirmed and heartbeats answered without a write
Why: A write's ReadIndex barrier waited on two log flushes: the leader's read round and its confirmation traveled only with a Ready, which its write out held back at depth 1, and a follower's heartbeat answer left only with no write out. RawNode::light_now now asks the round and gives the reads confirmed (LightReady::read_states, taken by Replica::take_light), and a member whose term and vote are durable answers a heartbeat at once, naming the durable end of its log and its durable commit (Raft::answer_beat_now), so its leader never counts a position past that member's durable log (Amphora's lane V3, AC-T1.8.3) The early answer states the member's incarnation as Raft::send does for every answer, so a member marked through a promise of its term still asks its leader where its log ends (R-8); the core's tests read the held channel the answer leaves by (lane V4).

